Z||000000||bzzzted||05-14-2001||05:12 PM||||has anyone here done a conversion like this? have read a good deal about it seems easy but unsure of whether i really need to buy a kit from companies like ACE?, or can i use mounts from the donor car?, as i have already sources out transmission mounts and related hardware., just need to figure out what it is that i will need to do to get the engine in there.  Help on experiences would be really helpful here!||||reg||5
Z||000001||MoneypitGT||05-14-2001||07:07 PM||||Working on a turbo QUAD 4 project right now, check out my site below. It's not too difficult, just make sure you have deep pockets. I am also working on making mounts to sell possibly for the motor. As far as the tranny goes you can use the stock mounts with out a prob. You will also need a throttle cable from an 86-88 4 banger fiero, and a fwd conversion kit from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com." TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com.</A>  The rest is nickel and dime parts, hoses, clamps and what not.<BR>Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects<p>[This message has been edited by MoneypitGT (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||14
